# General best practices

Numeric thresholds (refactor against these, not vibes):

- Method body: soft limit ~25 lines. Split if it does more than one thing.
- God Object: more than ~7 injected dependencies, crosses a layer boundary, or cannot be described in one sentence without "and".
- Widgets: prefer `StatelessWidget`. Extract from `build` when it mixes layout + parsing + I/O.

```dart
// BAD — God Object
class CoursesController {
  CoursesController(this.api, this.db, this.router, this.analytics,
      this.secureStorage, this.mapper, this.logger, this.locale);
}

// GOOD — split across UseCase + ViewModel + Mapper
```

- Inspect and reuse `lib/core/` and existing feature code before adding types.
- No unused files, no `TODO` placeholders in new code, no commented-out blocks.
- Forms: one field → a controller is enough. Three or more related fields or cross-field validation → the project's `reactive_forms` group (see `LoginFormGroup`). Do not invent a third form pattern.
- Destructive actions (delete) require the same confirmation UI already used in the app (`MyDialog` confirm). Do not skip confirmation.
- Public behavior changes need tests. Untested refactors start with characterization tests first.
